---
manual: styles.change
lines: [1123, 1128]
testability: interactive
display: any
expect: fail
reason: "Lacci's EditLine does not declare a :change style, so the proc is dropped with an 'Unexpected non-style keyword' warning (no ledger row yet; requested)."
----------- app code
Shoes.app do
  @said = para "nothing yet"
  @line = edit_line change: proc { @said.replace "changed" }
end
----------- test code
assert_equal "nothing yet", para("@said").text, "the handler waits for a change"

edit_line.trigger_change("typed")

assert_equal "changed", para("@said").text, "the proc given as the :change style ran"
